WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.312
Opportunity cost is the value of what is not done when time is spent somewhere else.

2
00:00:05.312 --> 00:00:10.008
It is easy to see the meeting, task, favor, or request that receives a yes.

3
00:00:10.008 --> 00:00:13.858
It is harder to see the quiet no that happens at the same time.

4
00:00:13.858 --> 00:00:24.636
Saying yes to a low-value commitment may mean saying no to focused work, maintenance, learning, recovery, family time, or a long-term goal that never becomes urgent.

5
00:00:24.636 --> 00:00:34.028
Some commitments are visible: meetings on the calendar, project deadlines, school events, operational handoffs, and promised deliverables.

6
00:00:34.028 --> 00:00:43.652
Others are hidden: preparation, context switching, travel, cleanup, emotional labor, coordination, and the recovery needed after intense work.

7
00:00:43.652 --> 00:00:47.501
Hidden commitments are where fantasy planning takes root.

8
00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:51.812
A plan looks reasonable because only the obvious work was counted.

9
00:00:51.812 --> 00:00:53.660
Tradeoffs are not failures.

10
00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.662
They are the normal shape of limited capacity.

11
00:00:56.662 --> 00:00:59.896
The problem comes when tradeoffs are accidental.

12
00:00:59.896 --> 00:01:02.590
Urgent work can crowd out important work.

13
00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.132
Maintenance can be deferred until it becomes a crisis.

14
00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:10.212
Learning can be postponed because no one is asking for it today.

15
00:01:10.212 --> 00:01:17.218
Relationships and recovery can be treated as flexible, even though neglecting them has real consequences.

16
00:01:17.218 --> 00:01:23.223
Deliberate choice means naming the cost before the calendar spends the time automatically.

17
00:01:23.223 --> 00:01:26.533
Before accepting a request, ask what it displaces.

18
00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:31.076
Before committing to a goal, ask what support and protection it needs.

19
00:01:31.076 --> 00:01:36.542
Before adding more, ask what should be reduced, paused, delegated, or made simpler.

20
00:01:36.542 --> 00:01:42.008
Opportunity cost does not make choices easy, but it makes the real decision visible.
